{
  "_doc": [
    "Declared authority for every REST route this plugin registers under wcb/v1.",
    "tests/test-route-authority.php walks the live registry and fails when a route is missing here,",
    "when an entry has no live route, or when the code's permission_callback differs from the one declared.",
    "audience: public = anyone, signed out included | member = any logged-in user, self-scoped |",
    "owner = the object's owner (or staff) | admin = a staff ability | guarded = a feature or ability gate resolved in the callback.",
    "A public route carries `reason` and `observed` (what a signed-out dispatch actually returned).",
    "A public GET route with an object id carries `probe`: the private fixture it is dispatched against, or `none: <why>`.",
    "An entry that exists only while a feature is on carries `conditional_on`: the setting key that mounts it.",
    "Closures are named Closure@<file> relative to the plugin root; Pro's pro_check() wrapper is unwrapped to its inner check."
  ],
  "standard": "~/.claude/skills/wp-plugin-release/references/authorization-guards.md",
  "routes": {
